WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.786
An automatic slideshow maker should take everything an editor decides and pull it

2
00:00:05.786 --> 00:00:07.500
straight from your data.

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:13.800
That means choosing which photos to use, setting their order and timing, writing a

4
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:19.716
script from the facts in each record, recording a voice, adding captions, and

5
00:00:19.716 --> 00:00:22.175
exporting every format you need.

6
00:00:22.175 --> 00:00:25.844
What it should not decide is whether a video goes live.

7
00:00:25.844 --> 00:00:29.931
Every finished video waits for a human to review it first.

8
00:00:29.931 --> 00:00:37.226
The source for each video is one record: a title, a set of facts, photo URLs in

9
00:00:37.226 --> 00:00:39.811
order, a status, and a link.

10
00:00:39.811 --> 00:00:45.496
Before anything renders, quality gates check that photos are sharp enough, that key

11
00:00:45.496 --> 00:00:49.331
facts are present, and that the item is still available.

12
00:00:49.331 --> 00:00:55.577
Videos can be queued in batches from a CSV or a sitemap, running unattended while a

13
00:00:55.577 --> 00:00:57.609
person reviews each result.

14
00:00:57.609 --> 00:01:03.141
When a price or status changes, the same record re-renders as a new version.
